.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-restore-unit 1  "tapectl-restore-unit " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-restore\-unit \- Restore a unit from a volume
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl restore unit\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-unit\fR> <\fB\-\-from\fR> <\fB\-\-to\fR> [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-scratch\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-overwrite\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-space\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restore a unit from a volume
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-unit\fR \fI<UNIT>\fR
Unit name
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Volume label
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Destination directory
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Tape device (by\-id path). Defaults to the only configured drive; required when more than one is configured
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Snapshot version to restore. Defaults to the newest version of the unit on this volume (the same rule RESTORE.sh applies); a version the volume does not carry is refused, naming the ones it does
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-scratch\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Where the restore\*(Aqs scratch directory is made (removed when the restore ends); defaults to inside \-\-to, never the system temp directory. A unit whose isolated catalogue from `stage create` is on disk streams its slices into dar and puts only named pipes there; otherwise (a rebuilt catalog, dar older than 2.7.9) every decrypted slice waits there, as large as the unit
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-\-overwrite\fR
Restore into a destination that already holds files, replacing any that collide. Without it a destination that is not empty is refused before the tape is touched
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-space\-check\fR
Skip the free\-space check (the unit\*(Aqs size when it streams; about twice that when its slices are spooled, with the scratch directory and \-\-to on one disk), for a filesystem that holds more than it reports free, such as a compressed or thin\-provisioned one
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be restored without restoring
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
